{"segments": [{"start": 0.0, "end": 5.7, "text": "she was making maybe $25,000 a year, but she lived in a college town. So it was pretty cheap"}, {"start": 5.7, "end": 12.88, "text": "in Northern California in Chico. And she ended up qualifying because who knew the bank will look at"}, {"start": 12.88, "end": 16.5, "text": "if you studied a certain thing and she studied marketing and then she got a job in marketing,"}, {"start": 16.52, "end": 21.7, "text": "they'll count your years in college as your two years experience. So just out of college,"}, {"start": 21.7, "end": 26.3, "text": "you know, she had this marketing job, she qualified for a $300,000 house. And she ended"}, {"start": 26.3, "end": 31.9, "text": "up finding a $250,000 house that needed work. She was willing to do that work. She did it all herself."}, {"start": 32.42, "end": 36.58, "text": "Then about, I don't know, a couple months later, there was a fire in the Chico area,"}, {"start": 36.96, "end": 40.7, "text": "there was families that needed to live in her house, the insurance company was willing to pay"}, {"start": 40.7, "end": 46.76, "text": "about $2,000 more than her expenses. So suddenly she was an investor overnight."}, {"start": 47.28, "end": 52.32, "text": "My point being don't go out and buy stuff, because that will throw off your debt to income."}, {"start": 52.32, "end": 55.6, "text": "If you if you drive up your credit cards and you go buy cars,"}, {"start": 55.6, "end": 61.72, "text": "this is going to affect your ability to actually buy real assets. So my baby girl listened to me,"}, {"start": 62.04, "end": 66.74, "text": "that house went up in value over $150,000. She ended up selling it and was able to buy"}, {"start": 66.74, "end": 71.14, "text": "in the Los Angeles area, a million dollar house because she had the $150,000 down payment."}], "words": [{"w": "she", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.22}, {"w": "was", "start": 0.22, "end": 0.32}, {"w": "making", "start": 0.32, "end": 0.56}, {"w"